  "question": {
    "text": "Two particles of equal mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>&nbsp;move in a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;under the action of their mutual gravitational attraction. The speed of each particle will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0065_ce2b8ffb586a.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 270px;\" /></p><p>Let speed of both the particles be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>.</p><p>Then, gravitational force between the particles will provide the required centripetal force.</p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced><mfenced><mi>m</mi></mfenced></mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>r</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>G</mi><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
